    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02715 does not stand and is refunded to the rider in full. No compensation is paid to the driver.\n\nWhat the record establishes. The driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 10:06:17 and EV-GPS-02715 places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from that moment: 44 qualifying fixes in one unbroken in-geofence run of 420 seconds, 10:06:17 to 10:13:17, against the 180 second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; no_show_threshold_sec is null, so no longer threshold cuts the dwell down). He cancelled at 10:13:19 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, a code POL-NS-01(d) recognises, with no boarding event and a null started_at. On the driver-side evidence alone POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) hold, no POL-NS-05 false-arrival issue arises (he was inside the radius, nowhere near the 300 m or 15 km/h trigger, so the clock needs no recomputation), and POL-NS-07 would fix his payout at SGD 3.60, being 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee (the fare ledger's derived money block states the same figure). The anti-farming check is clean: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the absolute limb of 4, and 1 against completed_trips_30d of 134 is a rate of 0.007, below the 0.08 limb; both limbs must trip together and neither does.\n\nWhy the fee is nevertheless refunded. POL-NS-04 displaces POL-NS-01 where three conditions hold, and all three hold here. (a) EV-CHAT-02715 carries two rider messages inside the waiting window - 'im at the pickup, which car are you? i cant see you' at 10:06:47 and 'hello? are you here' at 10:08:47 - both locating or coordinating on their face, and the log holds exactly the 2 messages trip_record.chat_message_count records, so nothing is missing from the exchange. (b) The driver posted no reply, both rider messages carry read_at null, and trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array; the cancellation came at 10:13:19, six and a half minutes after the first message, so the 120 second reply window had expired twice and no call was made. (c) The rider track inside EV-GPS-02715 has 67 of 67 qualifying fixes (not one filtered out), with a greatest distance of 20.89 m from the pickup pin and a mean of 17.66 m - well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider_presence_radius_m, and inside even the 50 m radius the driver's own arrival test uses. POL-NS-04 therefore exonerates the rider, refunds the cancellation fee in full and makes no driver compensation payable. The driver's statement that he 'waited the full time' is accepted as far as it goes and the trace confirms it, but waiting is not the test POL-NS-04 sets, and a driver who holds position while a rider about 21 m away messages him twice without answer has not met the coordination duty the clause enforces; the driver's own submission does not contest these coordination facts. POL-NS-01 is explicit that the fee stands only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces its limbs, and POL-NS-04 is that clause.\n\nEvidence integrity. Nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08. Clock skew is 0 seconds (the arrival event 10:06:17 coincides with the nearest fix); the trace holds 84 fixes, 100.0 percent coverage, a 10 second cadence, no gaps and a 0.0 second maximum gap, so POL-NS-08(b) is not approached; the chat log reconciles with chat_message_count; and the fare ledger's cancellation_fee line of SGD 4.50 equals the net fee produced by the resolution rule (platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact sits at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and no discounted- or impaired-evidence narration is engaged.\n\nThe missing traffic advisory. EV-ADVIS-02715-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; no advisory covers this pickup in this window. It is disclosed rather than relied on: it carries no fact, makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, and decides nothing here, the dwell being a single unbroken 420 second interval that needs no accumulation.\n\nEscalation and referrals. No POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged: the admissible artifacts do not contradict one another on arrival, dwell or rider presence; rider and driver disputes_with_counterparty_90d read 0 and 0 against the 2 limb (c) requires; rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0 against the 3 limb (d) names; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is clean; and the deciding facts rest on complete weight 1.0 artifacts, so limb (e) is not reached. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. No clause produces a referral on these facts, so referrals is empty. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes automatically on issue and reverses the rider's charge."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
