Escalation is not engaged under any limb of POL-NS-09. Limb (a) is not reached: the deciding facts rest on COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-GPS-02715, EV-CHAT-02715, EV-TRIP-02715, EV-FARE-02715), and confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor. Limb (b) does not apply: nothing in the record contradicts the arrival, dwell or rider-presence account - the driver's statement that he 'waited the full time' agrees with the trace. Limb (c) is not met (the same-pair dispute counters are 0 and 0, below the 2 required). Limb (d) is not met (rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 against the 3 named, and the POL-NS-07 check is clean). Limb (e) is not met: the trace shows 100.0 percent coverage, a 10-second sample interval, 84 fixes, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0, so it is unimpaired under POL-NS-08(b); the chat log holds exactly the 2 messages trip_record.chat_message_count records and is unimpaired under POL-NS-08(c); and the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so it is unimpaired under POL-NS-08(d). The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02715-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is not relied on by either side and decides nothing: POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable for want of a present and populated advisory, and the dwell is a single unbroken in-geofence interval with nothing to accumulate. No clause produces a referral on these facts - the arrival marker is true, so POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire, and the POL-NS-07 escalation does not trip. The monetary effect is SGD 4.50, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes on issue under POL-GEN-05."},"discarded_claims":[]}
